<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hibatullah Akhundzada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born c. 1961</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hibatullah Akhundzada is an Afghan cleric and Islamic jurist who became leader of the Taliban in 2016. After the Taliban took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> in August 2021 and restored the Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, he became its supreme leader. He governs from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a> by decree and has driven restrictive policies such as the bans on secondary and university education for girls and women.</p></div>
